<title>UK: Japanese Stocks in London lower, techs lose ground.</title>
<headline>Japanese Stocks in London lower, techs lose ground.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese stocks in London were mixed to lower on Monday as blue chip stocks weakened in the wake of profit-taking in high-tech issues in New York on Friday, dealers said.</p>
<p>In a half day session following a market and public holiday in Tokyo, the Nikkei/ISE fell 2.30 points to 1,662.13 as dealers took their cue from Friday's falls on Wall Street.</p>
<p>Shares in Sony Corporation fell 55 yen from their London close on Friday to finish at 10,622.5 yen, while shares in Canon Inc dropped 15 yen to 3,340 yen.</p>
<p>Dealers said shares in automotive company Honda Motor Co Ltd bucked the trend as investors took advantage of recent weakness in the stock. Honda rose 32.50 yen to 3,490 yen.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Langlands, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
